      "side": 1,
      "message": "FYI I\u0027ve tried this test on a Pixel6, and it passes for /default but fails for /strongbox.\n\nThe relevant part of the KeyMint spec is:\n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:hardware/interfaces/security/keymint/aidl/android/hardware/security/keymint/IKeyMintDevice.aidl;l\u003d279-281\n\nbut I think this is/was new for KeyMint.\n\nFor KeyMaster, the ACTIVE_DATETIME and USAGE_EXPIRE_DATETIME / ORIGINATION_EXPIRE_DATETIME tags were used for populating the validity period instead [1].  In practice, there were also default values of 0 (epoch) / 9999-12-31T23:59:59Z if these tags were not specified.\n\n[1]: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:hardware/interfaces/keymaster/4.0/IKeymasterDevice.hal;l\u003d665-670)\n\n",
      "revId": "aef42ba042e38deb6ba225f12de5d25237a161cd",
